5,1,1,talk,Shizue,,"Hello everyone. It is a pleasure to be here. Before we decide, perhaps we should ensure the chosen project is truly feasible? I believe checking the administrative records for potential bottlenecks would be very wise.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
6,1,1,talk,Ryuji,,I agree with Shizue. Theoretical brilliance is meaningless if the project lacks the practical means to be executed. We should verify the operational feasibility and resource availability before making our final selection.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
7,1,1,talk,Victoria,,I concur. It is easy to overlook the strain a new project places on shared infrastructure. We should examine the current state of our facilities to ensure they can actually support the proposed work.,"{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
8,1,1,talk,Benjamin,,A prudent suggestion. It would be a pity to award a masterpiece of a proposal only for it to wither due to administrative friction or hidden costs. Let us divide the records to be efficient.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
9,1,1,talk,Midori,,I agree with you all. It would be wonderful to ensure the researchers can focus entirely on their science without unexpected interruptions. Let's look into the records to see where delays usually happen.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
10,1,2,talk,Shizue,,I think it would be helpful to see which types of projects actually reached the finish line. Shall we divide the list so we don't overlap too much? I am happy to take whatever is left.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
11,1,2,talk,Ryuji,,"Since we are concerned with feasibility, I will focus on the human element. I'll examine the staffing rolls for technical posts and the minutes on secondments and crew strength to see who is actually available.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
12,1,2,talk,Victoria,,"I will focus on the infrastructure. I'll look into the accreditation and bookings at shared facilities, as well as the incident logs on shared instrumentation, to gauge current capacity and reliability.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
13,1,2,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall examine the travel and bench-fee lines in the ledgers, along with the national computing agreement and facility day rates. It is essential to understand the actual purchasing power of the award in today's climate.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
14,1,2,talk,Midori,,I'll look into the portfolio review of schedule overruns and the national repository deposit turnaround. I want to see where projects typically lose time and if there are systemic delays we should consider.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
15,1,3,talk,Shizue,,"That sounds like a wonderful division of labor. Since you have all chosen your areas, I will look into the closeout files of finished awards and the station records from partner field sites.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
16,1,3,talk,Ryuji,,"The distribution is logical. By covering staffing, infrastructure, finances, timelines, and historical outcomes, we will have a comprehensive view of the operational landscape. I am satisfied with this arrangement.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
17,1,3,talk,Victoria,,I agree. This comprehensive approach will allow us to identify any hidden risks. I look forward to seeing how our findings intersect when we reconvene.,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
18,1,3,talk,Benjamin,,Indeed. It is far more elegant to uncover a flaw now than to discover it through a failed project later. I believe we have covered all our bases quite thoroughly.,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
19,1,3,talk,Midori,,"I'm glad we're all on the same page. It feels like a very balanced approach, and I think it will really help us protect the researchers' time. I'm looking forward to seeing what we find.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
20,1,4,talk,Shizue,,I am glad we have such a thoughtful plan. Let us each take our time with the records. I look forward to hearing what you all discover; it will surely guide us to the right choice.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
21,1,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will proceed with my investigation. I believe the data on technical personnel will be the most critical factor in determining whether a proposal is a realistic plan or merely a wish list.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
22,1,4,talk,Victoria,,I will begin my review. Understanding the current pressure on our shared instrumentation will be key to determining if the infrastructure can truly sustain another high-demand project without compromising existing research.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
23,1,4,talk,Benjamin,,"I shall do the same. I am curious to see if the numbers still align with the promises made in the grant guidelines, or if the budget has become a mere formality. Until we meet again.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
24,1,4,talk,Midori,,I will start my review as well. I hope to find some clear patterns that can help us avoid unnecessary delays for the next awardee. I'll see you all soon!,"{""words"":30,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
