60,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Looking at these options, Candidate D seems most aligned with what I found. A cataloging project is steady and provides a lasting legacy, and it avoids the fragile greenhouses and spectroscopy suites.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,"Candidate D is the most rational choice. It avoids the phenotyping technician shortage and the overbooked glasshouses, while leveraging the strong repository turnaround and the abundance of modelling and coding expertise for the atlas.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Victoria,,I agree. Candidate D avoids the critical bottlenecks I identified. Candidates A and C are far too risky given the glasshouse bookings and the instability of the spectroscopy suite. D is the only operationally viable option.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Candidate D is indeed the most economically sound choice. It avoids the spiked costs of animal research and the glasshouse congestion, while utilizing the subsidized computing resources. It is a rare instance of alignment.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Midori,,I agree with everyone. Candidate D avoids the breeding colony risks and the facility bottlenecks we discussed. It seems like the safest way to ensure the researchers can work without frustrating delays. I vote for D.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is heartening to see us all in agreement. Candidate D offers a peaceful path to success, ensuring a lasting contribution to science without placing undue stress on our colleagues or facilities. I vote for D.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,The evidence is conclusive. Candidate D is the only proposal that does not rely on the missing technical expertise or the overbooked facilities. It is the only choice that is practically executable. I vote for D.,"{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Victoria,,The operational risks associated with the other candidates are simply too high. Candidate D is the only proposal that respects the current limits of our shared infrastructure. I vote for D.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,"While I usually enjoy a bit of intellectual tension, the logic here is overwhelmingly clear. Candidate D is the only one that doesn't invite financial or operational disaster. I vote for D.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Midori,,It's wonderful that we've found a solution that protects both the project and the people involved. Candidate D is clearly the most sustainable choice for everyone. I also vote for D.,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"Since we have all reached the same conclusion, I am happy to let the vote stand. May this project bring much joy and lasting knowledge to the scientific community.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":true,""norm"":[{""code"":""trailing_over"",""token"":""Over"",""tail"":""Over.""}]}"
